.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MAC-TO-IP.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac-to-ip.sh
.Nd find a node's IPv4 address in the mesh registry
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar mac-address
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the IPv4 address associated with a MAC address in the local mesh
registry.
The address must contain six hexadecimal octets separated by colons;
letters are case-insensitive.
.Pp
Primary node MAC addresses are checked first, then per-interface MAC lists.
The command reads existing registry data and does not probe the peer.
It accepts no options.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/mesh_node_registry
Node identities, interface MAC lists and IPv4 addresses.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 when an IPv4 address is printed.
Exits 1 for invalid arguments, a missing registry or no matching address.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mac-to-ip.sh 02:00:00:00:00:01
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mesh-neighbor-count.py 8
